      "en_why_17": "Why 1.7? ",
      "en_why_17_body": "Put ΔEN = 1.7 into Pauling's formula and you get 51% ionic character. The famous cutoff is just the halfway mark, picked for convenience. Nothing snaps at 1.7: Al–Cl (1.55) and C–F (1.43) sit right below it and behave like strongly polar covalent bonds, not salts.",
