      "off_by": "Not yet. The effort force is ",
      "ona_g35": "An onager has one arm instead of two. All the twisted rope pushes that single arm, and a sling on the end adds extra reach and speed.",
      "ona_g68": "One bundle, one arm. At the same winding it stores half what a two-bundle ballista does, but it only has to accelerate one arm instead of two, so a larger share of that smaller store reaches the stone. Adding a sling lengthens the payload radius and improves the share again. Store and efficiency are two separate things, and this machine trades one for the other.",
      "ona_g912": "Halving the store while halving the arm inertia is not a wash, because efficiency depends on the RATIO m_p/(m_p + m_eff) rather than on either quantity alone. In this model the onager typically shows a higher transfer efficiency than a ballista with the same arm mass, and a lower stored energy, so which one throws further depends on the stone. Lengthening the sling raises the payload radius and lowers the reduced arm inertia, which is the same lever argument the trebuchet makes.",
      "ona_k2": "One arm is held by a twisted rope. It swings up fast and bangs into a padded stop, and the stone keeps going.",
      "onager_sling": "Sling length",
      "open_bench": "Bench",
      "open_machine": "Build",
      "overlay_note": "Dashed arcs are earlier shots: ",
      "part_arm": "the throwing arm",
      "part_arm_n": "each arm is a lever turning about its bundle, trading a short powerful twist for a long fast sweep",
      "part_arm_n_k2": "each arm is a lever. The rope twists it back a little way, and the arm swings the stone a long way, fast",
      "part_arms": "the two spring arms",
      "part_beam": "the throwing beam",
      "part_beam_n": "long arm ÷ short arm, so the stone end travels that many times further than the counterweight end",
      "part_beam_n_k2": "the long end of the beam moves much further than the short end does, so the stone ends up going much faster than the weight",
      "part_ramp": "the loading ramp",
      "part_ramp_n": "rolling a stone up a slope instead of lifting it, which is the only way a crew moves it at all",
      "part_ramp_n_k2": "rolling the stone up a slope instead of lifting it straight up, which is the only way people could move it",
      "part_screw": "the bundle tensioning gear",
      "part_screw_n": "tiny turns against a huge load, which is how the springs are tuned at all",
      "part_screw_n_k2": "small turns of a screw against a very big pull, which is how you tighten the ropes just right",
      "part_stop": "the trigger and the padded stop",
      "part_tackle": "the cocking tackle",
      "part_tackle_n": "every extra rope segment halves the pull again and doubles the rope to haul in",
      "part_tackle_n_k2": "each extra loop of rope makes the pull half as hard, but you have twice as much rope to pull in",
      "part_trigger": "the trigger and the ratchet pawl",
      "part_trigger_n": "a small wedge holding an enormous force, and releasing it the instant you want it gone",
      "part_trigger_n_k2": "a tiny wedge holds back a huge pull, and lets go the moment you want it to",
      "part_winch": "the winch drum and handle",
      "part_winch_n": "a big handle circle turning a small drum, which is why one person can cock the machine",
      "part_winch_n_k2": "your hand goes round a big circle and the drum only goes round a small one, so one person can pull back a machine this big",
      "parts_g35": "Every part of this engine is one of the six simple machines from the Machine Shop. Tap one to go and try it on its own.",
      "parts_g68": "Nothing here is new. Every part is one of the six simple machines, and not one of them adds any energy: they only change the exchange rate between force and distance.",
      "parts_g912": "The engine is a composition of the six machines. Each contributes a mechanical advantage to a different stage, and the ones the tool models numerically show their live value here; the rest are present in the mechanism but not in the energy model.",
      "parts_k2": "This big machine is made of the small machines you already know.",
      "parts_title": "Simple machines in this engine",
